"Send throws: bytes out to a target that exists — TCP, UDP, TLS, HTTP, or a BLE write. Serve holds doors: listeners that answer whoever knocks, with an inbox for what arrives. The beacon is a name shouted into the air — a BLE advertisement carrying a payload, presence without a conversation. The GATT host is a shape worn in the air: services that can be discovered, read and written. Reach decides: a wire target wants Send or a knock; a room full of phones wants the beacon; a tool expecting a peripheral wants the GATT host." = "Send फेंकता है: bytes बाहर उस target तक जो मौजूद है — TCP, UDP, TLS, HTTP, या BLE write। Serve दरवाज़े थामता है: listeners जो दस्तक देने वाले किसी को जवाब देते हैं, आने वाले के लिए एक inbox के साथ। Beacon हवा में चिल्लाया गया एक नाम है — एक BLE advertisement जो payload लिए है, बातचीत के बिना मौजूदगी। GATT host हवा में पहना गया एक आकार है: services जिन्हें खोजा, पढ़ा और लिखा जा सकता है। Reach तय करती है: wire target को Send या दस्तक चाहिए; phones से भरे कमरे को beacon चाहिए; peripheral की अपेक्षा करते tool को GATT host चाहिए।";
